    2. Build output histogram grid (trivial from counts).
    3. For input, place objects on a 10x10 ORANGE grid. For each palette color with count>0, place that many 8-connected blobs (1-16 pixels) ensuring same-color blobs are Chebyshev-separated by >=2.
    4. Use random small shapes (single pixels, lines, L-shapes, plus signs, rectangles) for variety.
    5. Validate no two same-color components merge (re-check 8-connectivity after all placements).
